# NOTICE — third-party attributions

This project (pearlminer-sm89) is an sm89 / Ada Lovelace HiveOS packaging of
the REAL, open-source Pearl (PRL) miner **CPPminer**. The actual mining engine
— the CUDA cuPOW kernel, the stratum client, the proof encoder, and the share
submission code — is authored by the CPPminer project and is **not** written by
this repository's maintainer.

## CPPminer
- Upstream:    https://github.com/1640675651/CPPminer
- Pinned tag:  v1.0
- License:     MIT (see upstream LICENSE)
- What it provides: Pearl cuPOW backend (CUTLASS fused GEMM+XOR+jackpot,
  blake3 Merkle proof), `plain_proof` share encoding
  (base64(bincode proof), gzip for `type:"v2"` pools), stratum client tested
  against LuckyPool / Herominers / Kryptex, and the `--api-port` stats API
  used by `h-stats.sh`.

## Pearl (PRL) protocol references
- Pearl network / official miner: https://github.com/pearl-research-labs/pearl (ISC)
- Proof-of-Useful-Work from arbitrary matrix multiplication: arXiv:2504.09971
- Empirical study of Pearl's cuPOW protocol: arXiv:2606.04819

## What THIS repo adds
- HiveOS custom-miner packaging (`h-manifest.conf`, `h-config.sh`, `h-run.sh`,
  `h-stats.sh`) that maps HiveOS flight-sheet fields to CPPminer's CLI.
- A GitHub Actions workflow that cross-compiles CPPminer for `sm_89` and
  publishes an installable HiveOS tarball.
- `build-sm89.sh` for building on-rig.
- Flight sheets and documentation (English + Persian).

## CUDA runtime
The release tarball bundles `libcudart.so` from the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
(redistributable under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit EULA) so the miner runs on
HiveOS images that do not ship a CUDA toolkit install. The NVIDIA driver
(`libcuda.so`) is provided by the rig's driver and is NOT bundled.
